      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "Forecast Weather Influences: Mostly dry with very occasional snow flurries.  Fresh to strong South-East winds will increase to gale force early on Sunday, easing through the day and backing to become East-South-Easterly.\nObserved Weather Influences: A cold sunny day with light Northerly winds.  The freezing level rose to 900 metres by midday.\nObservedSnowStability: There is a cover of soft snow above 800 metres on all aspects. Isolated and localised accumulations of generally well bonded windslab were observed on North-Westerly aspects above 1000 metres. The avalanche hazard is Low."
